===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[stuffed]] [[shirt]]}}

# {{idiom}} One who is [[pompous]] or [[self-important]], especially one who is [[officious]] in a position of authority.
#* '''1914''', [[w:Samuel Hopkins Adams|Samuel Hopkins Adams]], ''The Clarion'', ch. 30:
#*: "Don't you come the high-and-holy on me. You and your smooth, big, phony '''stuffed-shirt''' of a father."
#* '''1952''', "[http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,859638,00.html Medicine: Mind Matters]," ''Time'', 26 May:
#*: Dr. Laughlin was the only one in a movie party who detested the second male lead—"I regarded him as overserious, pedantic, a '''stuffed shirt'''."
# {{usually|hyphenated}} Used [[attributive]]ly.
#* '''2000''', Frederik Balfour, "[http://www.businessweek.com/archives/2000/b3689207.arc.htm Return of a Hong Kong Highflier ]," ''BusinessWeek'', 10 July:
#*: The opportunistic style that was the bank's trademark still prevails and continues to attract talented young Hong Kongers looking for an alternative to the '''stuffed-shirt''' culture of most U.S. and European banks.

a person who evokes boredom
lacks humor about him or herself

